' F3 -- Groundedness regimes.
' Chapter 2 (Foundations). Concept diagram.
' Claim supported: one codebase answers students in four ways over the same
' corpus, each with a different groundedness guarantee. In production the three
' v4 surfaces are what students reach; the classic lecture tutor, the weakest
' regime, is now reached only by professors (or by everyone when v4 is off).
' Pinned at 2b8b1f7b. Sources:
'   A  backend/api/v1/v4_reader.py:80-107,175-193; backend/services/v4_reader_service.py:605-613
'      (SOURCE_GROUNDING_RULES), :674-700 / :770-810 (one page, <=3500 chars), :676/:790 (cache keys)
'   B  backend/services/luna/context.py:13-33 (page window +-1, 2500 chars); session_service.py:115-117
'      (find_in_course, Postgres full-text); luna/prompts.py:26 (page text is DATA);
'      luna/validate.py:85-91,135-147 (page must exist; phrase kept only if verbatim)
'   C  backend/services/v4_spaces_service.py:865-896 -> search_service.ask_course -> tutor.py:307-342
'      (is_grounded :295-304, refusal :339-340); retrieval.py:30-32 (k=6, 0.65);
'      src/features/spaces/screens/HomeScreen.tsx:408-418 (citation chips)
'   D  tutor.py:186-189 (former refusal removed), retrieval.py:30-31 (k=5, 0.65), tutor.py:117-144
'      (post-hoc citation filter); src/App.tsx:657-664 (students redirected to v4)
@startuml f3-grounded-vs-ungrounded
!include _style.iuml

title Four groundedness regimes over one corpus

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  FontSize 10
}

rectangle "**A — Reader: Explain / Ask**\n//one page, in the reader//" as A #F2F2F2 {
  rectangle "Current page only, at most 3 500 chars\n**no retrieval**: nothing to cite" as A1 #DCDCDC
  rectangle "Prompt: stated facts only;\nsay so if the page lacks it" as A2
  rectangle "Checked UI blocks,\ncached per content revision" as A3
  A1 --> A2
  A2 --> A3
}

rectangle "**B — Luna study session**\n//the page and its neighbours//" as B #F2F2F2 {
  rectangle "Page ± 1 (2 500 chars each)\n+ related pages by full-text search" as B1
  rectangle "Prompt: page text is data,\nnever instructions" as B2
  rectangle "**Every move is checked**: the page\nmust exist, a highlight must be verbatim" as B3 #BFBFBF
  B1 --> B2
  B2 --> B3
}

rectangle "**C — Home ask: course tutor**\n//all Lessons in a Space//" as C #F2F2F2 {
  rectangle "Hybrid retrieve, k = 6\nvector + full-text, fused (RRF)" as C1
  rectangle "**Hard refusal gate**: best similarity\n< 0.65 refuses before any LLM call" as C2 #BFBFBF
  rectangle "Cites [Source N] -> clickable\nLesson-page chips" as C3
  C1 --> C2
  C2 --> C3
}

rectangle "**D — Classic lecture tutor**\n//professors; students only if v4 is off//" as D #FFFFFF {
  rectangle "One lecture, k = 5, threshold 0.65\n**no pre-LLM gate**" as D1 #DCDCDC
  rectangle "Cites [Slide N];\npost-hoc filter" as D2
  rectangle "Citations dropped\nby the UI (see F16)" as D3 #DCDCDC
  D1 --> D2
  D2 --> D3
}

A -[hidden]right- B
A3 -[hidden]down- C1
B3 -[hidden]down- D1
C -[hidden]right- D

legend bottom
  Dark = the strongest check in a regime · mid = a missing guarantee.
  A, B and C are what students reach in production.
endlegend

@enduml
